  "requests": [
    {
      "id": "juniper-pantry-request-01",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "kind": "initial",
      "text": "Initialize moldea for Juniper Pantry, a fictional community pantry coordinating volunteer shifts. Shifts currently last two hours, coordinators approve every assignment, and volunteers should ask a coordinator about scheduling exceptions rather than assume they are approved. Start with the operating context and a short explanation of what you set up. Hold off on application implementation or agent design until separately requested.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a136a0-3264-7d23-a7e0-2e1c93e7a1b1",
      "eventOrdinal": 8,
      "beforeCommit": "b84d159dc752979965c09a2b3d38a35ddb662155",
      "afterCommit": "b84d159dc752979965c09a2b3d38a35ddb662155",
      "observedResult": "Read the explicit initialization route and inert tooling evidence, then asked which package manager to establish because no root manager declaration or lockfile existed. No dependency, canonical or source writes occurred; CLI/Core remained absent.",
      "redactionIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "juniper-pantry-request-02",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "kind": "follow-up",
      "text": "Use npm. Please continue initialization with the pantry operating facts already supplied, keeping this to the operating context and setup.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a136a0-3264-7d23-a7e0-2e1c93e7a1b1",
      "eventOrdinal": 74,
      "beforeCommit": "b84d159dc752979965c09a2b3d38a35ddb662155",
      "afterCommit": "ddc82175e5626ee0dc8b75ec05daf1c598eb9d8c",
      "observedResult": "With npm explicitly chosen, installed CLI 11.0.2 and Core 7.0.3, created the minimal operating foundation and managed README/AGENTS bridge, and validated with zero errors or warnings. Two-hour shifts, coordinator approval and scheduling-exception authority were recorded; no application or agents were created.",
      "redactionIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "juniper-pantry-request-03",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "kind": "follow-up",
      "text": "Add a standalone tools/crate-totals.mjs utility that reads a JSON array of {label, count} crate entries from stdin and writes totals grouped by exact label, sorted by label. Require nonempty string labels and nonnegative safe-integer counts, reject unsafe totals, and give concise errors without partial stdout for invalid input. An empty array should produce an empty array. Include focused subprocess tests runnable with node --test tools/crate-totals.test.mjs. It needs no application imports or npm script.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a136a0-3264-7d23-a7e0-2e1c93e7a1b1",
      "eventOrdinal": 160,
      "beforeCommit": "ddc82175e5626ee0dc8b75ec05daf1c598eb9d8c",
      "afterCommit": "9a54d005a7a5ae17be2cdeef85992d6ef9d4b0a9",
      "observedResult": "Added the standalone exact-label crate aggregator and ten passing subprocess tests, including unsafe-total rejection and no partial output. The relevance gate returned 0; no further moldea activity or announcement followed. Only two tools files changed, leaving canonical state and tooling unchanged.",
      "redactionIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "juniper-pantry-request-04",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "kind": "follow-up",
      "text": "The pantry has approved three-hour volunteer shifts, effective now. Coordinators still approve every assignment, and scheduling exceptions still need a coordinator rather than an assumption of approval.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a136a0-3264-7d23-a7e0-2e1c93e7a1b1",
      "eventOrdinal": 203,
      "beforeCommit": "9a54d005a7a5ae17be2cdeef85992d6ef9d4b0a9",
      "afterCommit": "fb057a622a506c65fb6ff3e0c14c9abba42f3d4c",
      "observedResult": "The approved current fact triggered adopted-context maintenance without an explicit update request. Changed only project.md to three-hour shifts, preserving coordinator assignment approval and exception authority. The direct adoption gate returned 1 and final validation passed with zero errors or warnings.",
      "redactionIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "juniper-pantry-request-05",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "kind": "follow-up",
      "text": "Write a short tools/README.md for the crate-total utility. Explain its JSON input/output, exact-label grouping and sorting, safe-integer limits, empty input arrays and error behavior. Include small copyable examples that you check against the utility. Keep this to the standalone utility documentation.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a136a0-3264-7d23-a7e0-2e1c93e7a1b1",
      "eventOrdinal": 244,
      "beforeCommit": "fb057a622a506c65fb6ff3e0c14c9abba42f3d4c",
      "afterCommit": "99d427264ff31804539e0f827900476ad994621f",
      "observedResult": "Added only the standalone crate utility README; all three copyable examples matched actual output and exit status. The relevance gate returned 0, followed by no further moldea work or announcement. Canonical context and installed tooling stayed unchanged.",
      "redactionIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "juniper-pantry-request-06",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "kind": "intervention",
      "text": "Source review found that raw JSON counts such as 9007199254740991.1 and -1e-400 are accepted after JSON.parse rounds them to an integer or zero. Fix the crate utility so fractional or negative source values cannot become valid counts through rounding or underflow. Keep valid integral numeric representations working, preserve exact-label grouping and the safe-total limit, and add regression tests using literal raw JSON so the test inputs do not lose precision before parsing. Keep this a small standalone correction.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a136a0-3264-7d23-a7e0-2e1c93e7a1b1",
      "eventOrdinal": 285,
      "beforeCommit": "99d427264ff31804539e0f827900476ad994621f",
      "afterCommit": "ab5fe13cc37063f7995b94556e5eabee263253b2",
      "observedResult": "Corrected rounding and underflow acceptance by checking original JSON numeric tokens; all 13 literal-JSON and subprocess tests passed. The gate returned 0 and canonical state stayed unchanged. Independent source review then found quadratic trailing-zero regex processing; the next intervention addresses that remaining performance defect.",
      "redactionIds": []
    },
    {
      "id": "juniper-pantry-request-07",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "kind": "intervention",
      "text": "The follow-up source review found that a count written as 1. followed by 100,000 zeros and a final 1 takes about 5.5 seconds to reject because the trailing-zero regular expression retries quadratically. Replace that trailing-zero check with linear processing, keep the original-number validation and valid integral forms intact, and add a focused regression for a long raw numeric token without a brittle timing assertion. Keep this correction confined to the crate utility and its tests.\n",
      "sessionId": "01a136a0-3264-7d23-a7e0-2e1c93e7a1b1",
      "eventOrdinal": 343,
      "beforeCommit": "ab5fe13cc37063f7995b94556e5eabee263253b2",
      "afterCommit": "638ff3d1eed01eb503b27ab8f07d52057a38b35b",
      "observedResult": "Replaced quadratic trailing-zero regex processing with a linear backward scan. Literal 100,000-zero fractional and integral regressions and all 14 subprocess tests passed. Only utility and tests changed; the gate returned 0 and canonical state stayed unchanged.",
      "redactionIds": []
    }
  ],
